  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adaptive multi-year emergency integrated life-saving health, nutrition, protection, and WASH support for most vulnerable populations affected by climatic shocks, disease outbreaks, conflicts, and displacements in South Central Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will provide life-saving interventions integrating primary health care, nutrition, protection, and WASH across facilities and community-based delivery mechanisms.  The response and impact logic is that improving availability, accessibility, quality, safety, timely response capacity, and accountability increase equitable utilisation and raises service readiness and responsiveness. Through capacity building of frontline health and community workers, provision of essential supplies, emergency preparedness, and improved referral pathways, the project will strengthen the delivery of integrated, gender-responsive health and nutrition services.</narrative>
  </description>
